  "title": "IEEE 802.11: Fix format truncation",
  "description": "What oui_base_custom actually prints to the buffer depends on\nMAXNAMELEN, and is definitely quite a bit less than ITEM_LABEL_LENGTH.\nNo truncation has actually been occurring, but gcc warns if other\ncustom base labels put its return value is put in a larger buffer and\nthen use snprintf to add even more bytes.\n\nFor safety verify with a static assertion the relative sizes of the\nbuffers.\n\nPing #20175",
